{
  "title": "108: al-Kawsar الكوثر",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ ٱللَّهِ ٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nإِنَّآ أَعْطَيْنَٰكَ ٱلْكَوْثَرَ (1)\nINNAA A-A’TAYNAAKAL KAWSAR.\nVerily We have given thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) The ‘Kawthar’ (Abundance)\nفَصَلِّ لِرَبِّكَ وَٱنْحَرْ (2)\nFASALLE LE-RABBEKA WAN-HAR.\nSo pray thou unto thy Lord! and offer sacrifice\nإِنَّ شَانِئَكَ هُوَ ٱلْأَبْتَرُ (3)\nINNA SHAANE-AKA HOWAL ABTAR.\nVerily, thy enemy shall be the one cut off (in his progeny)",
  "merits": "There are 3 ayaat in this ‘Makki’ Surah. It is narrated from Imam Ja’far as-Sadiq (a.s.) that the person who recites this Surah in any of his prayers, will drink from the fountain of Kawsar. The reward for reciting this Surah is compared to ten times the number of cattle slaughtered on Eid-ul-Azhaa every year until the Day of Resurrection."
}
